# aws_fwflash config

config AMAZON_AWS_FWFLASH
    tristate "AWS firmware flash driver"
    depends on X86_64
    help
      Say M here to enable the AWS firmware flash driver (aws_fwflash).

      This driver provides a character device (/dev/aws_fwflash) with a
      restricted IOCTL interface for triggering Software Management
      Interrupts (SMI) and accessing physical memory regions. It is used
      by the aws_fwflash userspace tool to perform in-band firmware updates,
      replacing the deprecated /dev/mem and ioperm() mechanisms which are
      disabled on Amazon Linux 2023+ for security hardening. Access to the
      device requires CAP_SYS_RAWIO and the node is created mode 0600.

      To compile this driver as a module, choose M here.
      The module will be called aws_fwflash.
